{"name":"Calypso","hex":"#3d7188","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Calypso","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Orchidaceae – a single species of orchid Calypso bulbosa (fairy slipper orchid)."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A sea nymph who entertained Odysseus on her island, Ogygia, for seven years.","The eighth moon of Saturn."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Calypso"}],"entries":[{"title":"Calypso (mythology)","blocks":[{"text":"In Greek mythology, Calypso was a nymph who lived on the island of Ogygia, where, according to Homer's Odyssey, she detained Odysseus for seven years against his will. She promised Odysseus immortality if he would stay with her, but Odysseus preferred to return home. Eventually, after the intervention of the other gods, Calypso was forced to let Odysseus go."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Jan_Styka_-_Kalipso.jpg/330px-Jan_Styka_-_Kalipso.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calypso_(mythology)","wikidata":"Q48961"},{"title":"Calypso (nymphs)","blocks":[{"text":"In Greek mythology, Calypso is the name of several nymphs, the most well known being:"},{"items":["Calypso, the nymph who, in Homer's Odyssey, kept Odysseus with her on her island of Ogygia for seven years. Calypso, who fell deeply in love with Odysseus, was only swayed to release him after Athena convinced Zeus to send the order."]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calypso_(nymphs)","wikidata":"Q106311126"},{"title":"Calypso (comics)","blocks":[{"text":"Calypso Ezili is a supervillain appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics. Created by writer Denny O'Neil and artist Alan Weiss, the character first appeared in Amazing Spider-Man #209. Calypso is a voodoo priestess of Haitian descent. She serves as an adversary of the superhero Peter Parker / Spider-Man. The character is the occasional lover and partner of Kraven the Hunter. Calypso is also known as The Witch and The Hunter of Souls."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1a/Calypso_Ezili_%282019_Design%29.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calypso_(comics)","wikidata":"Q2934584"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Beckmann_-_Tiedemann%2C_0646.jpg/500px-Beckmann_-_Tiedemann%2C_0646.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Beckmann_-_Tiedemann%2C_0646.jpg/500px-Beckmann_-_Tiedemann%2C_0646.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Odysseus and Calypso, painted by Max Beckmann, 1943","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeckmann_-_Tiedemann%2C_0646.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Calypso_-_L%27%C3%8Ele_de_Calypso.png/330px-Calypso_-_L%27%C3%8Ele_de_Calypso.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Calypso_-_L%27%C3%8Ele_de_Calypso.png/330px-Calypso_-_L%27%C3%8Ele_de_Calypso.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACalypso_-_L'%C3%8Ele_de_Calypso.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Calypso_and_Odysseus_-_L%27Odissea.png/120px-Calypso_and_Odysseus_-_L%27Odissea.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Calypso_and_Odysseus_-_L%27Odissea.png/250px-Calypso_and_Odysseus_-_L%27Odissea.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/